\f1\fs22 Halo found the Ruined Castle facility the very antithesis of industry or commerce; it was aesthetically pleasing, and minimalist without being austere. It felt welcoming and warm, almost homey due to the a subtle use of warm timbers that framed expanses of wall cladding. At the corners of corridor junctions where coloured strips, maybe twelve centimetres by two, stacked like rungs on ladders with a centimetre between. At each corner there was a ladder on each wall. The colours were muted and warm\'97even the green, Halo noted\'97\
